Package: mbmm
Title: Mechanistic Bayesian Mixture Models for Latent Kinetic States
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Linh", "Do", email = "thuylinh.do@duke.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Janice", "McCarthy", role = "aut"),
    person("Bruce", "Rogers", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates how a covariate shifts the probability of a latent
    biological state that is expressed through a longitudinal trajectory
    rather than observed directly. Each state is represented by a population
    of mechanistic trajectories (a "bank"); integrating a censoring-aware
    trajectory likelihood over that population gives a class likelihood, and
    a covariate-dependent gate supplies the prior state probability. An EM
    algorithm estimates the gate by weighted logistic regression on the
    resulting posterior responsibilities, so participants whose state is
    uncertain contribute at the weight the evidence warrants. Includes the
    eclipse-phase target-cell-limited viral model and the reduced Andraud
    prime-boost antibody model used in the accompanying manuscript.
